      "text": [
        ": سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنِ اَلْمَرْأَةِ يَتَزَوَّجُهَا اَلرَّجُلُ مُتْعَةً ثُمَّ يُتَوَفَّى عَنْهَا هَلْ عَلَيْهَا اَلْعِدَّةُ قَالَ \"تَعْتَدُّ أَرْبَعَةَ أَشْهُرٍ وَ عَشْراً فَإِذَا اِنْقَضَتْ أَيَّامُهَا وَ هُوَ حَيٌّ فَحَيْضَةٌ وَ نِصْفٌ مِثْلَ مَا يَجِبُ عَلَى اَلْأَمَةِ\" قَالَ قُلْتُ فَتُحِدُّ قَالَ \"نَعَمْ وَ إِذَا مَكَثَتْ عِنْدَهُ يَوْماً أَوْ يَوْمَيْنِ أَوْ سَاعَةً مِنَ اَلنَّهَارِ فَقَدْ وَجَبَتِ اَلْعِدَّةُ وَ لاَ تُحِدُّ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4606 - Safwan ibn Yahya narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Al-Hajjaj, who said:\nI asked Abu Abdullah (as) about a woman who entered into a Mut'ah (temporary marriage) and then her husband passed away.\nImam (as) said: \"She must observe an 'Iddah (waiting period) of four months and ten days.\"\nThen Imam (as) continued: \"If her term ends while he is still alive, her waiting period is one and a half menstrual cycles, similar to what is required for a female slave.\"\nI asked: \"Does she need to observe mourning (Hadd)?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"Yes, but if she stayed with him for a day, two days, or even just an hour during the day, the waiting period becomes obligatory, but mourning (Hadd) is not required.\""
        ]
      }
    },
